.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt LCC-DESKTOP 1
.Os 1.6.2

.Sh NAME
.Nm lcc-desktop
.Nd configure desktop plugins and desktop icons.

.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h | -help
.Op Fl v | -version
.Op Fl s | -screen Ar number

.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is part of the Lumina Control Center.
It manages the utilities embedded on the desktop of one screen: plugins can
be added and removed.
It also controls whether the contents of the Desktop folder and icons for
removable media are shown on the desktop.

.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display help on command line options.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Display version information.
.It Fl s Ar number , Fl -screen Ar number
Configure the desktop on screen
.Ar number ,
counted from 0.
The default is 0.
.Nm
exits with an error if the screen does not exist.
.El

.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl % lcc-desktop --screen 1
Configure the desktop on the second monitor.

.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/lcc-desktop
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lumina-desktop/desktopsettings.conf
Desktop and plugin settings shared with
.Xr lumina-desktop 1 .
.El

.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lcc 1 ,
.Xr lcc-panels 1 ,
.Xr lcc-wallpaper 1 ,
.Xr lumina-desktop 1

